[General] Two problems in this block:

1. `create(record, clientId, bootstrapServers)` has no callers left after this PR — `KafkaProducerTelemetry` and `KafkaProducerInstrumentation` both pass a cluster id now.
2. The `String clusterId` and `Metadata kafkaMetadata` overloads differ only in the type of the last argument. `create(record, clientId, servers, null)` doesn't compile (ambiguous), and the two call sites read identically, which is easy to get wrong later.

The `Metadata` variant only exists because `KafkaUtil.clusterIdFromMetadata` is package-private. Making that method public (see the comment on `KafkaUtil`) lets the advice resolve the id itself and collapses this down to one factory. The `org.apache.kafka.clients.Metadata` import added on line 11 then becomes unused and should go too.

```suggestion
  public static KafkaProducerRequest create(
      ProducerRecord<?, ?> record,
      @Nullable String clientId,
      @Nullable String bootstrapServers,
      @Nullable String clusterId) {
    return new KafkaProducerRequest(record, clientId, bootstrapServers, clusterId);
  }
```

