[Testing] `.as(...)` descriptions aren't used in this repo's tests, and `assertThat(stream.anyMatch(...)).isTrue()` reduces a failure to "expected true but was false". `anySatisfy` keeps the offending points in the failure output:

```suggestion
      List<MetricData> metrics = testing().metrics();
      assertThat(metrics)
          .anySatisfy(
              metric ->
                  assertThat(metric.getData().getPoints())
                      .anySatisfy(
                          point -> {
                            String id = point.getAttributes().get(KafkaClusterId.ATTRIBUTE_KEY);
                            if (expectedClusterId != null) {
                              assertThat(id).isEqualTo(expectedClusterId);
                            } else {
                              assertThat(id).isNotEmpty();
                            }
                          }));
```

Two more things about this test: because it branches on `metricsReporters.isEmpty()`, in javaagent mode it never exercises `onUpdate` at all despite the name, and only checks that *some* point happens to carry a non-empty id. And `testProducer` is created for its observables, but the reporter that receives `onUpdate` is `metricsReporters.get(size - 1)`, which isn't guaranteed to be the one belonging to that producer.

