`LegacyKafkaConsumer` is in `org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer.internals`, not `org.apache.kafka.clients.consumer`, so this entry never matches any class. The 3.7+ delegate `AsyncKafkaConsumer` is missing too, and in Kafka 4 the legacy delegate was renamed `ClassicKafkaConsumer`. As written, native-image users get no consumer cluster id on exactly the versions the delegate lookup was added for.

